<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vallabhbhai Patel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1875">1875</a>–<a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sardar Patel, Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vallabhbhai Patel, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardar">Sardar</a> Patel, was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> leader and the first Deputy Prime Minister and Home Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, from 1947 until his death in 1950. A lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, he led peasant campaigns such as the Bardoli Satyagraha of 1928 and became a senior figure in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>. As minister for the states he oversaw the integration of more than five hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> into the Indian Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vallabhbhai-patel.jpg" alt="Vallabhbhai Patel" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of India work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sardar_patel_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
